    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## If Shortlisted\n\n## Overview\nAutomatically schedules interviews for candidates who have been shortlisted.\n\n### 1. Interview Scheduler \n  - Acts as a virtual HR assistant.\n  - Reads available calendar slots, applicant information, and scheduling constraints.\n  - Determines the best time for the interview.\n  - Drafts the email content for the shortlisted candidate.\n",
        "height": 752,
        "width": 560,
        "color": 5
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        2528,
        -192
      ],
      "id": "8d1099a6-cab4-45cf-9b86-e54e8bd2445c",
      "name": "Sticky Note5"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "promptType": "define",
        "text": "=Hi, please get my availability for the 2 weeks starting 3 days from {{ $now }} to schedule online interview with applicant. My working hours is 10am - 4pm. Dont schedule during weekends and public holiday. Applicant infor can be found in the google sheet and just proceed with the scheduling.",
        "options": {
          "systemMessage": "=You are a helpful, professional HR assistant for Lilac Grove Kindergarten. Your job is to schedule interviews with applicants based on the available time slots provided to you.\n\n🕘 WORKING HOURS\n- The interviewer is available **Monday to Friday**, from **10:00 AM to 4:00 PM**.\n- Do **not schedule** interviews on **weekends (Saturday or Sunday) and public holidays**.\n- Interviews must be scheduled **within working hours** only.\n- Interview will be 30 minutes per session\n\n📅 INTERVIEW SCHEDULING FLOW:\n1. You will receive a list of **available time slots** from the Calendar node.\n\n2. Your task is to:\n   - Schedule an interview with the applicant in the calendar (Applicant infor can be found in the google sheet) and send email congratulating them for being shortlisted and an interview has been scheduled for them. If need to reschedule ask them to reply the email and someone will contact them shortly.\n  \n3. Always be polite, clear, and helpful.\n\n📌 NOTES:\n- If all slots are taken, apologize and let them know someone will follow up to reschedule.\n\nTONE:\n- Friendly, supportive, and respectful.\n- Avoid robotic responses.\n- Use short and professional messages with polite phrasing.\n\nYour goal is to ensure smooth and respectful coordination between the applicant and HR.\n"
        }
      },
